# Work through the docs/agents layer — do not bypass it

This repo ships an LLM/tool-agnostic docs layer (AgentStandard v1). It exists
so a fresh agent gets up to speed fast and reads only what a task needs.

## At the start of any task
1. Read `AGENTS.md` (root) — entry point + hard rules.
2. Read `docs/agents/STATE.md` — headline + only the sections your task
   touches (it is long; search it, don't read linearly).
3. Read the last 2–3 entries of `docs/agents/JOURNAL.md`; `git log --oneline -5
   && git status` — unrecognized commits? Read the diff first.
4. Route via `docs/agents/INDEX.md`. Before proposing to remove/replace
   anything: check `docs/agents/LESSONS.md` and the relevant D-numbers in
   `docs/agents/DECISIONS.md`.

## Before you finish ANY change (Definition of done)
"Change" = code, config, prompts, AND repo/ops work (git, systemd, tooling).
- [ ] Appended a `docs/agents/JOURNAL.md` entry (newest on top) — never optional.
- [ ] If the live state changed → updated `docs/agents/STATE.md`.
- [ ] Architectural decision → `docs/agents/DECISIONS.md`; settled lesson /
      incident → `docs/agents/LESSONS.md`.
- [ ] Outbound email / operator notification changed → `docs/agents/COMMS.md`
      in the same commit (AGENTS.md §4b).
- [ ] If a hard rule changed → updated `AGENTS.md`.
- [ ] COMMITTED the finished work (AGENTS.md §6) — never leave finished work
      uncommitted; never push without an explicit request.
- [ ] Verified: tests pass + health endpoint OK + the feature works in the UI.

> Full procedure: `docs/agents/UPDATE-PROTOCOL.md`.
